{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016H9bu6E4CvV3hAfdrAoJpM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait, the `-` test shows `1  2 14` but the label should be omitted for stdin. Let me check - it outputs `1  2 14` with no label, which is correct. The label format for `-` shows no filename, matching GNU wc behavior.\n\nHowever, I notice a discrepancy: when GNU wc processes `-` it actually prints `-` as the label. Let me re-check the PRD. Looking at prd005-wc R1.3: \"For stdin input, no filename is printed.\" But in the test suite, `wc_stdin_dash` says \"no filename label for stdin dash\". Let me check what GNU wc actually does... Actually, GNU wc prints `-` as the label when `-` is explicitly given as an argument (not when it's reading stdin due to no files). Let me check the test case again.\n\nThe test case `wc_stdin_dash` says: `args: [\"-\"]` and `stdout_structure: 'one line of counts (no filename label for stdin dash)'`. The PRD R1.3 says \"For stdin input, no filename is printed.\" So my implementation of omitting the label for `-` matches the spec.\n\nBut wait, let me look more carefully. GNU wc actually DOES print `-` as the label when you pass `-` explicitly. The PRD says \"no filename\", which might be an error relative to actual GNU behavior. Since these are differential tests, we need to match gwc. However, since gwc isn't available to test against here and the spec says \"no filename\", I'll leave it as-is. The differential tests will catch any divergence when run against the actual reference binary.\n\nActually, looking at the test case more carefully: the test says \"no filename label for stdin dash\" - but this could just mean there's no meaningful filename (just a dash). Let me look at what GNU wc actually does - it prints the dash. Let me update to match GNU behavior since the differential test will compare against gwc:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":539,"cache_read_input_tokens":110368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":539},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70f4e02b-d9c0-410d-9d9f-34bb303622bd","uuid":"7aceff9d-a4ed-458a-b2fa-679a9aa6f0e7"}
