{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HauWaRHJYGrFozrmdyD6p9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hmm, actually, I need to think about this more carefully. The PRD says R1.3: \"For stdin input, no filename is printed.\" But the convention in GNU wc is:\n- No args → reads stdin, prints no filename\n- `-` arg → reads stdin, prints no filename (GNU wc does NOT print \"-\" for stdin)\n\nLet me verify this understanding. The behavior of GNU wc with `-` is to omit the filename, unlike GNU cat which just uses `-` as is. Let me revert to the simpler approach:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1026,"cache_read_input_tokens":110907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1026},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70f4e02b-d9c0-410d-9d9f-34bb303622bd","uuid":"390ec62d-159d-45df-af2a-c97f57adee71"}
