{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TpSQ1SEur4mEc1fJ5N6Thy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tasks are complete. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nCreated `cmd/wc/main.go` implementing prd005-wc R1-R6:\n\n**Counting modes (R1-R2):**\n- Default: lines + words + bytes when no flags given\n- `-l`: newline byte (0x0A) counting\n- `-w`: word counting via `unicode.IsSpace` boundaries\n- `-c`: byte counting\n- `-m`: character (rune) counting with invalid UTF-8 bytes counting as one character each\n- `-L`: max line length with tab expansion to next multiple of 8\n- Fixed output order: lines, words, chars/bytes, max-line-length (regardless of flag order)\n\n**Multi-file and total modes (R3):**\n- Dynamic column width right-alignment across all files and total\n- `--total=auto` (default), `--total=always`, `--total=only`, `--total=never`\n\n**Special inputs (R4):**\n- `-` treated as stdin filename\n- Binary input handled without corruption\n- Empty input produces zero counts\n- `--files0-from=FILE` reads NUL-delimited filenames\n\n**Error handling (R5-R6):**\n- Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on file errors (still processes remaining files)\n- SIGPIPE handler for clean exit (matching `cmd/cat` pattern)\n\n**Acceptance criteria verified:**\n- AC1: `go build ./cmd/wc/` succeeds\n- AC2: Default mode produces correct `2 3 12` output\n- AC3: Combined flags produce fixed output order\n- AC4: Two-file input with per-file and total lines\n- AC5: `--total=never` and `--total=only` work correctly\n- AC6: Non-existent file prints error, exits 1, processes remaining files\n- AC7: Empty stdin produces `0 0 0`\n- AC8: `go vet ./cmd/wc/` passes with no diagnostics"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":114913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":343},"output_tokens":1,"ser